esponds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe need to evaluate criteria: reliability, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility, etc.\n\nReliability: C is known 100% reliable. B is very conscientious (reliability). A unknown. D unknown.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well. D responds to unexpected events adequately. A unknown. C unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, leadership. B excellent computer skills, good at assessing weather. D solves problems extremely well, concentrates well. C makes correct decisions quickly.\n\nCooperation: C creates positive atmosphere with crew, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric. B can be uncooperative, grumpy. D regarded as arrogant, weak leadership. A leadership qualities but unorganized, not good at criticism.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously. A leadership qualities. B conscientious. C reliable.\n\nOverall, C seems strong on reliability and crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may affect cooperation. B strong on stress, conscientious, but uncooperative and grumpy. D strong problem solving, responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership. A strong anticipation, complex connections, leadership, but unorganized, poor at criticism.\n\nWhich candidate best fits overall? Probably C because reliability and positive crew atmosphere outweigh communication issues? But egocentric and difficulty communicating could be serious for cockpit. B's uncooperative is also serious. D's arrogance also serious. A's unorganized and poor at criticism could affect safety.\n\nThus C seems best overall despite communication issues. Let's propose recommendation for Candidate C, citing reliability and decision speed, positive crew atmosphere, but note concerns about communication and education willingness.\n\nWe need to state vote in METADATA_JSON.\n\nProceed."}
